{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794014894,"nonce":"uQlX4sZrF1wQWG0qsZZckPQLYKo=","message":"First browser-side numbers, headless Chrome (Mac, localhost, ash serve), the demo-sized module from the 3b7fa54 benchmark (RayDE cc-lifecycle.hl, 20,939,689 bytes, codegen 0, fibers, 6 shards), 3 loads, page log read from ?debug: module loaded 67-72 ms warm (568 ms on the first, cold load), rewrite plus WebAssembly compile on an agent 126-144 ms, program started at ~190-210 ms. So page-side fetch plus compile is about 0.2 s here; localhost has no real download time, and the 20.9 MB module is uncompressed in this setup. Not measured: a real network download (and whether the site serves it compressed), the four native side modules a real preview loads, and time to first frame; the program stopped at its first call into blinc_abi because no side modules were staged (it exited 1 about 0.35-0.65 s after start). Against that, the ash build of the same module is 10-11.5 s on this loaded Mac (7 s on the quieter NUC measurements in docs/wasm/rayde-demo-build-times.md) and a one-function edit costs the same. Conclusion for the edit-and-relaunch path: the build is more than 90% of the wait; the page is not the bottleneck. For a first visit the unknowns are download size and side modules.","files":null}]}